# finish/glyph: T6's light on P (STYLE_P2 27.3, 27.7; P2C_CONTRACTS 3b, 6b; LADDER-FINISH, ladder polish i1 + i2): ONE readable
# shape of light a piece, big enough to breathe at 1x, never a scatter of specks. ! Glow 2 (saturated), : Glow 3, ^ Glow 4
# (absolute: light is light); k = the shield's DEVICE paint one step down (polish i2: steel-blue under the T6 starmetal
# cross, dark amber under the Mythic's gilt lattice; i1's metal-1 face turned the Mythic's lattice into a grey grille).
# Keys glyph<w>x<h>, FIT-centred on the part's P box (the largest view that fits).
# Shields (polish i2, the panel: "the T6 halo, gems and glints are 1-2 px sparks, invisible at game scale"): every shield
# map paints its device's stem down the face's centre column (device paint, outside P), so the light FLANKS it (the P cells
# either side, Glow 2, a Glow 3 tip at the top) and device + light read as one cross of light 3 px wide that breathes at 1x;
# the 7-wide heater faces (5x7 5x8 7x8 7x9 7x10 8x8; 4x7 4x8 edge-on, 2x6 2x7 slung) flank the arms above the boss too.
# The blade's flat (9x9 10x9 8x9 6x9 9x6 9x5 5x9 6x6 5x5 6x3 9x1 1x9 7x1 5x1; 7x7 = the guard-grip diagonal, shared with
# the round shield as a saltire, and painted nowhere else so the blade keeps its steel) is lit end to end with a dark beat
# every 3 px. Brow bands (12x2 10x2 12x1 10x1): ONE light round the brow gem, never two dashes either side of it (i1's
# dashes read as a pair of eyes on the T6 great helm). Breastplate panels carry a 3 px ridge of light at most.
# Ladder polish i3 (the panel: "the breathing is not perceptible at 3x; only the shield gem reads"): the shield face below its
# top two rows is g = Glow 1 (the device's own dark step, absolute) instead of k, so the whole face breathes with the cross
# as one band of light (T6 deep cyan, the Mythic ember); the top rows keep k so lt6's soft light stays inside C13's 320.
# Measured: lt6 DRAWN bright 62, soft 256-320; lt6m DRAWN bright 93, soft 129-174. Generated by gen_i3.py (i3).
# Budget (C13, polish i2): lt6 DRAWN 47 sprite-bright px (112 max), soft 264; lt6m DRAWN 104 bright, soft 334 (the
# Mythic's flame aura is ~270 of it: LADDER-FINISH asks kMaxSoft 360). Stacks over finish/filigree (a clear cell falls
# through to the gold). Generated by LADDER-FINISH's gen_polish.py (i1) and gen_i2.py (i2).
# Alloys i1 (LADDER-FINISH, A5 "T6's living finish too subtle at game scale"): every T6 piece carries a band of light that
# breathes in every facing, not only the shield: the brow bands (12x1 10x1, and row 0 of 12x2 10x2) are ONE diadem of light
# across the brow, Glow 1 at the ends, Glow 3 beside the gem (the Jade masked helm, spangenhelms and great helms: before, 4 px);
# 9x2 (a great helm's side band, a shield's rim seen edge-on) the same band; the spear's leaf (3x2 at the diagonals, 2x3 and
# 2x2 upright) a ridge of light (before: none, its P cells fell between the drawn strokes); 3x3 a 3 px column (was 2).
# Measured (rpg_test --doll-ladder --finish): lt6 bright 104 / soft 101-164 (unchanged), lt6w 54 / 50-121, imp6's soft light
# 34 -> 40+ (C13's "must read at 1x" now passes); C12-C14 0 failed. Generated by gen_a.py (alloys i1).
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i2) fits for the smallest panels the forge styles leave (1x1, 1x2, 1x3, 2x1: the fluted chest's valley, the plackart seen from the side, a cop's heart), so every style takes its tier finish.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.glyph
legend ! glow 2
legend : glow 3
legend ^ glow 4
legend k device 1
legend g glow 1
tags tile overlay fit
on-region P

